00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.155
- [Voiceover] Kelsey asks:
"What are your thoughts on

00:00:37.155 --> 00:00:39.649
"starting to share content
before you're an expert?

00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:41.802
"Do you wait, or do you
share your journey?"

00:00:42.743 --> 00:00:44.773
- Kelsey, that's an interesting question.

00:00:44.773 --> 00:00:46.834
First of all, I think
this whole expert thing

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.553
is a ridiculous notion.

00:00:48.553 --> 00:00:49.343
Am I an expert?

00:00:49.343 --> 00:00:50.091
Are you an expert?

00:00:50.091 --> 00:00:51.351
Are you an expert?

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.837
You know, I mean when does one get to

00:00:53.837 --> 00:00:54.913
claim they're an expert?

00:00:54.913 --> 00:00:56.681
I mean, I thought I was
an expert when I was 22.

00:00:56.681 --> 00:00:59.017
I'm pissed that I wasn't
able to make these videos

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:01.273
when I came out the
gate in '98 and brought

00:01:01.273 --> 00:01:03.386
serious thunder to the wine world.

00:01:03.386 --> 00:01:07.063
You would have saw a young,
raw, hungry, angry Gary Vee,

00:01:07.063 --> 00:01:09.196
and that would have been really
interesting to look back on.

00:01:09.196 --> 00:01:11.311
So I say map that journey, baby

00:01:11.311 --> 00:01:14.342
because the truth is,
expert is subjective.

00:01:14.342 --> 00:01:16.142
I've seen people tweet
that I'm a bigger expert

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.790
than people I think are way
more accomplished than me,

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:20.403
and then other people put me
in tweets with other people

00:01:20.403 --> 00:01:21.833
that I clown every day of the week.

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:24.176
More value in this pinky than them.

00:01:24.176 --> 00:01:27.116
So expert is clearly subjective
and, more importantly,

00:01:27.116 --> 00:01:30.347
here's the real punchline,
put that content out

00:01:30.347 --> 00:01:32.637
because you're gonna be able
to look back at that content,

00:01:32.637 --> 00:01:33.925
your grandkids are gonna be able

00:01:33.925 --> 00:01:35.275
to look back at that content.

00:01:35.275 --> 00:01:37.736
Plus you will see things,
and how they evolve.

00:01:37.736 --> 00:01:41.808
My 1998 video would have
been: "In 2002, every single

00:01:41.808 --> 00:01:44.302
"person's gonna go into
a store with a cell phone

00:01:44.302 --> 00:01:46.406
"'cause they're blowing
up in London right now,

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:49.031
"and they're gonna come in
and be able to tell the price

00:01:49.031 --> 00:01:52.749
"of every single product, so
sell your products at cost."

00:01:52.749 --> 00:01:55.220
And that would have been a big no, wrong.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.646
That would have been fun to look at.

00:01:56.646 --> 00:01:58.612
So, there are no experts

00:01:58.612 --> 00:02:01.232
except if the audience
deems you an expert,

00:02:01.232 --> 00:02:03.499
if somebody deems you an
expert as young talent

00:02:03.499 --> 00:02:05.504
out the gate, then kudos on you.

00:02:05.504 --> 00:02:07.494
Start filming now.

