00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:43.388
- [Voiceover] Andrew asks:
"How do you change the culture

00:02:43.388 --> 00:02:45.985
"to one of genuinely
caring about the customer

00:02:45.985 --> 00:02:48.665
"when the current ethos
is so established?"

00:02:48.665 --> 00:02:49.758
- Andrew,

00:02:50.468 --> 00:02:51.378
Andrew.

00:02:51.378 --> 00:02:52.988
There's only one way to change the culture

00:02:52.988 --> 00:02:55.395
when it's broken to something genuine.

00:02:55.395 --> 00:02:57.095
Kill leadership.

00:02:57.095 --> 00:02:59.811
Leadership is in charge of the culture.

00:02:59.811 --> 00:03:02.201
Everything, my friend, stems from the top

00:03:02.201 --> 00:03:03.994
when it gets into the DNA.

00:03:03.994 --> 00:03:06.412
So do not let the leader,
the CEO, the board,

00:03:06.412 --> 00:03:10.141
whoever it may be, do not let
her, him, make an excuse that

00:03:10.141 --> 00:03:12.218
something is happening
below in middle management,

00:03:12.218 --> 00:03:14.838
or some other things,
because she's in charge,

00:03:14.838 --> 00:03:17.312
he's in charge of that middle management.

00:03:17.312 --> 00:03:19.945
Every problem at VaynerMedia, is my fault.

00:03:19.945 --> 00:03:21.569
Right here, you're looking
right at this face.

00:03:21.569 --> 00:03:23.514
It's my fault because I
empower everybody else

00:03:23.514 --> 00:03:26.300
to create that culture, and
so how do you change it?

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.324
You change the top, and if the top owns it

00:03:28.324 --> 00:03:29.744
'cause it's the family business,

00:03:29.744 --> 00:03:31.640
or just became the new CEO,

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:32.950
and it's not going to
change, then you need

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:34.587
to get the hell out of there
because the only people

00:03:34.587 --> 00:03:36.686
that can change culture are
the people from the top.

00:03:36.686 --> 00:03:38.607
It's true you can hack from the bottom,

00:03:38.607 --> 00:03:40.275
you can maybe then inspire the top, but

00:03:40.275 --> 00:03:42.960
that top still has to make the decision.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.320
That is the judge of culture.

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:48.961
- [Voiceover] Saura asks:
"How do you book speaking

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.025
"engagements when you
aren't well known yet?"

00:03:53.105 --> 00:03:54.726
- Saura, they way I booked
speaking engagements

00:03:54.726 --> 00:03:57.712
when I wasn't well known yet
was, I did them for free.

00:03:59.232 --> 00:04:01.471
The entitlement that you are not known,

00:04:01.471 --> 00:04:02.766
you do not deserve to get paid.

00:04:02.766 --> 00:04:04.562
Do you know why you get paid to speak?

00:04:04.562 --> 00:04:06.525
Because you put asses in the seats.

00:04:06.525 --> 00:04:08.755
Because people want to come and see you.

00:04:08.755 --> 00:04:11.137
The reason I get astronomical
speaking fees is,

00:04:11.137 --> 00:04:14.479
knock on wood, zoom in
here, lemme knock on wood,

00:04:14.479 --> 00:04:16.988
knock on wood, I am very
fortunate to have an

00:04:16.988 --> 00:04:19.411
audience that wants to travel
and go to these events,

00:04:19.411 --> 00:04:21.620
and that's why you get
justified those fees.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.530
You don't get paid if you're
not bringing any value,

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.364
so either your content is phenomenal,

00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:28.523
but even then if you're not
putting asses in the seat

00:04:28.523 --> 00:04:30.580
you are not getting paid,
so the best way to do it

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.173
is to do what I did,
in my opinion, which is

00:04:33.173 --> 00:04:36.049
I spoke for free in the
beginning, quite a bit,

00:04:36.049 --> 00:04:38.138
to establish my name, to show everybody

00:04:38.138 --> 00:04:41.456
how good I was at it, and then
the demand side came to it.

